What Is the Lithium Metal Anode Market?
Lithium metal anodes are battery negative-electrode materials that use metallic lithium or lithium-containing alloy structures instead of conventional graphite-based anodes. Their high theoretical specific capacity makes them an important area of research for next-generation rechargeable batteries.

These materials are being investigated for electric vehicle batteries, energy storage systems, consumer electronics, and specialized aerospace applications. Commercial development focuses on improving electrode stability, controlling lithium deposition, reducing dendrite formation, and enabling consistent manufacturing of thin lithium foils and protected electrode structures.

